An error about a file found under a directory names the file by its listed path, in normal form (`input/broken.md` for the argument `./input/`), while the glob view's first line keeps the argument as given.
== args
./input/
== file input/broken.md escaped
\xff
== file input/ok.md
# Ok
== stdout
glob view: ./input/
input/ok.md (1 line): # Ok
== stderr
File input/broken.md is not UTF-8 text
== exit 1
